        {
          "id": "formate_ch_stretch",
          "label": "ν(CH)",
          "symmetry": "A₁",
          "note": "The C-H bond stretches — the key HCOO* marker band, since no other common surface species shares this exact C-H environment. Can fall into Fermi resonance with the δ(OCH)+νₐₛ(OCO) combination band, splitting into a doublet. The free formate ion has its own conventional ν-numbering in the vibrational-spectroscopy literature (this mode is commonly cited as ν₁), though the exact assignment order varies by source more than CO₂'s does.",
